# PX4 parameters for a MAGNETOMETER-DENIED GPS-denied run.
# Format: <vehicle_id> <component_id> <name> <value> <type>  (type 6 = int32, 9 = float)
#
# Apply ON TOP OF gps_denied_ekf2.params + sitl_bringup.params:
#   droneflight px4-params --file configs/px4/gps_denied_ekf2.params \
#                          --file configs/px4/sitl_bringup.params \
#                          --file configs/px4/mag_denied.params
# then paste the `param set` lines into pxh and `reboot`.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The 2026-07-22 dropout arm measured 12.40 deg of EKF2 heading error inside the
# 3 s vision gaps (vs 2.07 deg outside). But EKF2 only held it to that by falling
# back on the magnetometer: `cs_mag_3d` went 0.0% -> 39.4% during the gaps. In
# SITL the magnetometer reads PERFECT TRUTH, so that 12.40 deg is a best case and
# the dropout result is quietly optimistic.
#
# A covert GPS-denied aircraft cannot assume a trustworthy magnetometer — near
# ferrous structure, power lines, or deliberate interference it is degraded or
# useless, and heading is precisely the axis a magnetometer is there to anchor.
# Denying it makes external vision the ONLY heading observation, which is the
# honest configuration for testing what a vision dropout actually costs.
#
# ⚠️ CONSEQUENCE: with EKF2_EV_CTRL=11 (position H+V + yaw), vision is now the
# sole heading source. During an EV dropout EKF2 has NO heading observation at
# all and runs on gyro alone. That is the point of the test — and it is why the
# bridge must be publishing BEFORE arming (RUNBOOK 3b.3), since EKF2 has nothing
# else to align yaw against.
#
# ⚠️ VERIFY THE ENUM ON YOUR BUILD BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE. The meaning of
# EKF2_MAG_TYPE has changed across PX4 releases. At pxh:
#       param show EKF2_MAG_TYPE
#   and check the value list in QGC's parameter view (or `param info`). 5 = None
#   on v1.14+; if this build disagrees, fix the value here rather than in your
#   shell history, or the next run silently re-enables the magnetometer.

# Magnetometer fusion OFF (5 = None). This is the parameter that actually
# removes the heading anchor from EKF2.
1	1	EKF2_MAG_TYPE	5	6

# Tell the rest of the stack there is no magnetometer, so preflight checks do not
# refuse to arm over a sensor we are deliberately ignoring.
1	1	SYS_HAS_MAG	0	6

# Disable the magnetic-field consistency check. With no mag fusion it has nothing
# to check, and left on it can still block arming.
1	1	EKF2_MAG_CHECK	0	6
